{"posts":[{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1126","t":"My Home Work 3: USDJPY_H4 DBR &RBD","a":"ajentha","d":"","n":"#1126","p":46,"im":["4d5c699bd660b91ab1b0d0f3268baed9c7e45a06"],"m":1126},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1127","t":"My HW 4: USDCHF_H4 DBR & RBD","a":"ajentha","d":"","n":"#1127","p":46,"im":["d42b5d7d2842790ea55b0312f3d6c624e47f96df"],"m":1127},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1128","t":"My HW 5: GBPUSD_D1 RBD & DBR","a":"ajentha","d":"","n":"#1128","p":46,"im":["abf55aee7244b25aae1533200d5c7e2193b539cf"],"m":1128},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1129","t":"Hello All,\n\nSecond batch of homework below for Caps and DBR's/RBD's. Thank you.","a":"pipscout","d":"","n":"#1129","p":46,"im":[],"m":1129},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1130","t":"","a":"pipscout","d":"","n":"#1130","p":46,"im":["7ace4fd57721a09526d6baafe61ae6e892721ff3","46ff99abc66f2f9a41731cf313ee05dd2b1c91b8"],"m":1130},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1131","t":"","a":"pipscout","d":"","n":"#1131","p":46,"im":["b0804436987a6068168da1c196e8f79ad061b6ee","5387fc9177e54c85a8c891d3485e55873fe6af74"],"m":1131},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1132","t":"Hello Everyone,\n\nHere is the next group. Through about 160ish with these.","a":"pipscout","d":"","n":"#1132","p":46,"im":["eca8740080b3e05a30de6fbfbe35de244bd3b407","7c37fb2794cf005bd3349f690c2dab0dc209600b"],"m":1132},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1133","t":"Hello All,\n\nThis is about 220ish about, I think. If I am doing it correctly, I have to say it is a very helpful exercise. Thanks.","a":"pipscout","d":"","n":"#1133","p":46,"im":["72d0bd7ddc6549c822db903aed0e1f08d38dfce4","c2dfbc086bf9e67c0b380e8943b50e3d45cca48f","caaaf71c116c18b24b6e905721500c5c03077353"],"m":1133},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1134","t":"My Home Work: 6 RBD & DBR","a":"ajentha","d":"","n":"#1134","p":46,"im":["4d5c699bd660b91ab1b0d0f3268baed9c7e45a06"],"m":1134},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1135","t":"My Home Work 7: USDJPY_D1 for RBD &DBR","a":"ajentha","d":"","n":"#1135","p":46,"im":["0bdf51923af8c2c12f7613df149b61beab413962"],"m":1135},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1136","t":"My HW 8: EURJPY_H1 RBD & DBR","a":"ajentha","d":"","n":"#1136","p":46,"im":["d4eb46bdd0a55124e93966620a90a7ad97838663"],"m":1136},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1137","t":"HW 9: EURNZD_D1 RBR & DBR\n\nHW 10: EURNZD_H1 RBR & DBR","a":"ajentha","d":"","n":"#1137","p":46,"im":["bee999dbf2e656b581f2eb6aac4473a5655dfb56","e582b6c628bb069a8668f24f440a0f7a7cea440f"],"m":1137},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1138","t":"My Home Work 11: RBD & DBR","a":"ajentha","d":"","n":"#1138","p":46,"im":["4a28f98496bfe435203fe3a6af174a900b7979bd"],"m":1138},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1139","t":"HW4","a":"fxsniper","d":"","n":"#1139","p":46,"im":["25f19a8bcffdd26f527780ba7951243c59b187f8"],"m":1139},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1140","t":"Hey there Sniper, Just a little something that you might find useful","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#1140","p":46,"im":["ffe20a3d2b710158f42449f5a558db82a210ab30"],"m":1140},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1141","t":"Hey there ajentha, just a little something to point out when you see an areas/zone get overtaken (Eng)\n\nP.S. This is for post #1126","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#1141","p":46,"im":["8b46aaa608ffd46da36c3c7923a668607cce7805"],"m":1141},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1142","t":"Hello everybody!\n\nI will start posting my homework, I ask you to correct me if I'm doing wrong!\n\nThank you!","a":"pedroampires","d":"","n":"#1142","p":46,"im":["cfc4669195d29519ba1b3fd61dc3e5eaf6a8fa3f","f12db3530bfd4635fedea2c3fd2f8b0b108c771b","c3edbd9d78c1b31cedd3c77e8c50dfa1ef86eb6f"],"m":1142},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1143","t":"Some more example in USDCHF...","a":"pedroampires","d":"","n":"#1143","p":46,"im":["58a4b68a27c65f62b694b4402be467ec2f342b6b","cf5f2d87c13e80a4d386fd7ad5bc1c3d27ccf4df","b914ee1bf88b9b9520d28a6db87f0716e551c6e5"],"m":1143},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1144","t":"Good day to you all, These are the last batches of my homework on DBR/RBD-Price caps (132-201). Your kind comments are highly welcome. I have been thoroughly blown away by the information available on this forum and the wonderful people who have been altruistic in supporting each other to become better traders. Remain bless.","a":"tamodu","d":"","n":"#1144","p":46,"im":["27163d8009c51cdd0455063aae2ffd3d892eca72","07347459d6f9d5d3c8b6e18d557222fee9cfff41","0f4e32cc8c43bf04e4c5244739d9b6e83438a9f8","66519c34985e44775961a51995a72de3794ab33a"],"m":1144},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1145","t":"Hello everyone, After a long break from preparing homework, and spent many hours reading materials in an attempt to understand the price movement, I go back and start all over again... Start an exercise aimed to show the most points of supply and demand. I'd love to get your comments.","a":"adishal","d":"","n":"#1145","p":46,"im":["8b5d416fbfba4d37270ad309cdd3d2935f03d357"],"m":1145},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1146","t":"Finally starting my homework, its long overdue.\n\nDon't want to get too crazy with marking all the stuff on the chart so I've only marked what I think are the important ones and noted the reaction with FTB. There are many new FTRs generated upon reaction to the original zones but I'm trying to keep the chart clean and rather than just mark out 200 of these guys I want to try and get 200 important ones.\n\n1)RBD (from the 5M) and small FO which causes a QM level and reacts to the pip on return ( not shown). 2) DBD DP to break into the compression to the left reacts on return. 3) RBD FTR from entrance into compression on the left reacts FTB. 4) DBD formed in the middle of compression to the left not surprising, it gets faked on return (compression is a PAZ so we are interested in the edges of the zone). It ends up being a flip zone. 5) DBR current cap on price strengthened by the engulf of 4. Price reacts on return. 6) DBR 15M base of move up. Price compresses into base forming a nice QM and we are also in H4 demand. 7) this DBR is a point of interest as its the last tiny pocket of demand left before entering the new CP zone. It reacts on FTB (DBD on 5M) is engulfed and then produces a FTR from the other side proving it still holds relevance as a zone on our chart (the boxes are drawn approximately on the 15M). #8 is a very important RBD as it is the top of compression so once engulfed it makes the DBR at 9) worthy of a trade even though it has been tested as we are coming from HTF supply and we have broken into a new zone and will test higher maybe even continue on up to the next H4 supply.","a":"antraxia","d":"","n":"#1146","p":46,"im":["f8c859f7e2ea370beb8a020385d8046e9a585e11","cd51571f0cdbd7ccb23285fa6ab8533c5b3d94b4"],"m":1146},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1147","t":"This is my homework Example of DBR and RBD on GBPNZD H4.. Just feel free to comment..","a":"em1blitz","d":"","n":"#1147","p":46,"im":["24b8c2377063e2bcb0190fe9795dc2622dbb9a5f","ba5cb1227f507249118fc43bcd671521623d0cb7","9fe50304552e76d87e119b711c639240f10f7d8e","04c7020da848a7a35d0e92a344ca042fe1d87125"],"m":1147},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1148","t":"hi i am new want to see if i mark the area correctly?","a":"andron20","d":"","n":"#1148","p":46,"im":["746cbf1c3548f94ef8f2d63725b2650aeec08d63"],"m":1148},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1149","t":"Here are some screenshots of the Caps on Price homework. I have uploaded a screenshot for each time frame using different pairs. I used red for RBD and blue for DBR. I would greatly appreciate any feedback on this work. I hope that I am spotting the caps on price correctly. I don't think I have reached at least 200 caps on price yet, so I will continue to find some more.","a":"maani1990","d":"","n":"#1149","p":46,"im":["8c571f9e3540ae219cb40c5ec7f96a28e34b069a","221e88b9b4eef059ea908f781a3fb630e3f3250e","b931d0bef9cdccf731d8d67aa873ecd508374fd4","669c6940d632beac4a10014eb9856192a20e9a38","81f6689d3096fca95816dc00a2ed36fecb27466a","884025130947adc7581191714b1c55d41ab1824e","6abfdc2b54d55783ce0ee63fcd4f7c4512ed31ae","dd9c26bcbb5603ab732545d74c456b3ed5ae18dc","2080b67de249de4b6fc4e35e443755845289a232"],"m":1149},{"id":"dbrrbd_p46_1150","t":"andron20 wrote: hi i am new want to see if i mark the area correctly?\n\nandron20 - Hi, I am by no means an expert at this, but I believe your demand area you have drawn hasn't been correctly drawn. This is what I think it should look like, but feedback from more experienced traders would help here. This is just my opinion. Also your DBR and RBD are not all clear. do you mean that is where they start and the head to your supply and demand, base and bounce?","a":"maani1990","d":"","n":"#1150","p":46,"im":["746cbf1c3548f94ef8f2d63725b2650aeec08d63","c67a128a635f307ed392b94daa26e83cebdefc0c"],"m":1150}],"images":[{"k":"4d5c699bd660b91ab1b0d0f3268baed9c7e45a06","t":"assets/thumbs/4d5c699bd660b91ab1b0d0f3268baed9c7e45a06.webp","f":"assets/images/4d5c699bd660b91ab1b0d0f3268baed9c7e45a06.png","w":1023,"h":681,"b":28178,"o":"4d5c699bd660b91ab1b0d0f3268baed9c7e45a06.png","p":46,"pid":"dbrrbd_p46_1134"},{"k":"d42b5d7d2842790ea55b0312f3d6c624e47f96df","t":"assets/thumbs/d42b5d7d2842790ea55b0312f3d6c624e47f96df.webp","f":"assets/images/d42b5d7d2842790ea55b0312f3d6c624e47f96df.png","w":1023,"h":684,"b":28514,"o":"d42b5d7d2842790ea55b0312f3d6c624e47f96df.png","p":46,"pid":"dbrrbd_p46_1127"},{"k":"abf55aee7244b25aae1533200d5c7e2193b539cf","t":"assets/thumbs/abf55aee7244b25aae1533200d5c7e2193b539cf.webp","f":"assets/images/abf55aee7244b25aae1533200d5c7e2193b539cf.png","w":1018,"h":652,"b":18759,"o":"abf55aee7244b25aae1533200d5c7e2193b539cf.png","p":46,"pid":"dbrrbd_p46_1128"},{"k":"7ace4fd57721a09526d6baafe61ae6e892721ff3","t":"assets/thumbs/7ace4fd57721a09526d6baafe61ae6e892721ff3.webp","f":"assets/images/7ace4fd57721a09526d6baafe61ae6e892721ff3.jpeg","w":1363,"h":610,"b":78587,"o":"7ace4fd57721a09526d6baafe61ae6e892721ff3.jpeg","p":46,"pid":"dbrrbd_p46_1130"},{"k":"46ff99abc66f2f9a41731cf313ee05dd2b1c91b8","t":"assets/thumbs/46ff99abc66f2f9a41731cf313ee05dd2b1c91b8.webp","f":"assets/images/46ff99abc66f2f9a41731cf313ee05dd2b1c91b8.jpeg","w":1359,"h":617,"b":84273,"o":"46ff99abc66f2f9a41731cf313ee05dd2b1c91b8.jpeg","p":46,"pid":"dbrrbd_p46_1130"},{"k":"b0804436987a6068168da1c196e8f79ad061b6ee","t":"assets/th